The vulnerability occurs when the second message containing the actual assets arrives before the first LZ Message. In such a scenario, when `_finalizeDeposit` is invoked to swap the dummy tokens for actual ETH within the deposit pool, it relies on `msg.value` to determine the amount of ETH to swap.

However, as the LZ message has not yet arrived, there are no dummy tokens available, resulting in a situation where `_finalizeDeposit` lacks the necessary dummy tokens to send to `swapETHForAssetWithinDepositPool`. Consequently, the call to `swapETHForAssetWithinDepositPool` may result in an incomplete synchronization process.

## Remediation

Ensure the function utilizes the current ETH balance of the contract instead of relying solely on `msg.value` to determine the amount of ETH available for swapping.

